{"_id":"0gUVJh8x12q9aLTU","name":"Green Torch","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:green-torch","level":16,"monsterType":"Plant","intelligence":"None","perception":"Magic","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Forests, Mountains, Plains","reputation":20,"weakness":25,"weakPoint":"Fire damage +3 damage","initiative":21,"movementSpeed":"5 (Creep)","fortitude":"20 (27)","willpower":"19 (26)","source":"CR III p. 360","description":"This plant mimics settlements and ruins lined with simple buildings. The plant is a giant flower with a radius of about 30 meters, with six petals that open in a radial pattern. Mimicry is achieved by deforming the numerous tentacles that line the petal's surface. Still, there is also an element of magical illusion, and the monster is assumed to have been modified during the Magic Civilization Period. In the center of each petal is a stamen with a greenish light at the tip. To the uninitiated, it looks like a tower of green lights that brightly illuminate the entire settlement. This light is due to the same effect as the symbiotic organisms of the Lunoicos .\n\nDuring predation, the tentacles on the surface of the petals break their mimicry, bunch together, and strike at moving objects. The central stamen also attacks using its luminescent ability. The roots beneath the petals must be eliminated in order to defeat it, making it a troublesome monster that should be treated with caution.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Mimicry/25/Danger Sense/Negates","description":"It mimics uninhabited settlements and ruins. While mimicking, characters cannot perform a Monster Knowledge check on this monster. If a character approaches it unintentionally, they need to make a Danger check with target number 25, and if it fails, they will be surprised (see CR I, p. 144). Mimicry will be automatically ended once the monster starts to act.\nThis monster can be detected with [ Sense Magic ]."},{"title":"◯ Psychic Immunity","description":"Roots"},{"title":"◯ Under the Petals","description":"Any character wishing to attack or interfere with this monster must roll 1d at the beginning of its turn. If the number of 1d is not greater than the number of Petal sections of this monster alive, the Roots section of this monster cannot be chosen as a target, including those affecting a wide area, and cannot become a target for that turn. Exceptions are magic and effects that have \"Range: 2 (Infinite)\" and do not require visibility."},{"title":"► Nutrient Replenishment","description":"Select any Petal sections with HP of 1 or more, and heal their HP by 60 points. Roots can arbitrarily allocate the HP in units of 10 points."},{"title":"► Nutrient Augmentation","description":"In the turn, when this ability is used, the Stamen section will be able to perform [ ► Light Wave] twice.\nStamen"},{"title":"► Light Wave/20 (27)/Evasion/Negates","description":"With \"Range/Area: 2 (30m) / Shot ,\" deals 2d+16 energy magic damage to \"Target: 1 Character\".\nPetal"},{"title":"► Undulating Petals/20 (27)/Fortitude/Negates","description":"The entire petal undulates violently, shaking the character standing above it. The character is knocked prone within \"Range: Caster,\" dealing 2d+25 physical damage to \"Target: 1 area (6m Radius) /2 0\". Flying, floating, and other characters that do not have their feet on the ground are not affected by this effect.\nOnly one Petal section can use this unique skill each turn."},{"title":"► Confusing Scene/20 (27)/Willpower/Negates","description":"Petal's tentacles disorient the surrounding characters.\nAll characters within \"Range: Caster\" and \"Target: All Areas (30m Radius)/All\" should roll 1d. If the roll is \"1-2\", the character cannot take a Major Action on their turn for 10 seconds (1 round). This effect does not apply to characters other than with five senses perception.\nOnly one Petal section can use this unique skill each turn.\n2d |\nLoot |\n2 - 6 |\nLightly Glowing Pollen (770G/Gold Green A) |\n7 - 10 |\nGlowing Blue Pollen (1,370G/Gold Green S) |\n11+ |\nWhite Green Pollen (7,370G/Gold Green S) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Green Torch","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"1WQm8uzy17ctM5df","name":"Green Cemetery","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:green-cemetery","level":9,"monsterType":"Plant","intelligence":"None","perception":"Magic","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Ruins","reputation":18,"weakness":21,"weakPoint":"Fire damage + 3 points","initiative":0,"movementSpeed":"-","fortitude":"13 (20)","willpower":"12 (19)","source":"CR II p. 367","description":"This is a mottled, glowing moss that clings to the outer walls of ruins. The moss and its spores refract light, creating illusions for approaching characters.\n\nThe illusion cannot directly harm, but while it is perceived as a threat, the spore poison slowly drains the target's strength, leading to death.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Wall Moss","description":"It cannot fall prone, nor is it affected by any effect that moves its position (coordinates or area). Also, it is immune to Throw attacks."},{"title":"◯ Limited 2 Actions","description":"Can perform a Major Action twice in one round. However, it is limited to one each of [ ► Illusory Light] and [ ► Toxin Spores]."},{"title":"◯ Inviting Light/12 (19)/Willpower/Negates","description":"It produces light that attracts creatures.\nAny character within a 50m radius of this monster (in Simplified Combat, all areas) must perform a Willpower check at the start of their turn. If this check fails, the character tries to get as close as possible with its Normal Move. The character can choose any actions they want to make (actions that can only be made with a Limited Move are not allowed).\nA character already in the same position (coordinates or area) as Green Cemetery is not affected."},{"title":"► Illusory Light/Can't","description":"It gives a hallucination, so it fights with itself to \"Target: 2-3 areas (10m Radius) / All\" and \"Range: Caster.\"\nThe target must immediately perform an Accuracy check, a Spellcasting check, or a Performance check (the one with the highest standard value). Then, the same target must counter it with an Evasion check or Willpower (those who have mastered the combat feat [ Counter ] may use an Accuracy check) and compare the success value against each other.\nThe target is unaffected if there is a tie or the opposing side's success value is higher. However, if the opponent fails to do so, the target is knocked prone by the illusion. In addition, the target will not be able to move or take a Major Action on its turn.\nIn this comparison of success values, all permanent effects or duration apply to both checks. In the opposite Evasion check or Willpower check, it is possible to use an item to affect the check."},{"title":"► Toxin Spores/11 (18)/Fortitude/Half","description":"Sprays Toxin Spores within \"Range: Caster\" and \"Target: 1 area (6m Radius) / All\", and deals 2d+8 poison magic damage to the targets.\n2d |\nLoot |\nAlways |\nGreen Dye (80G/Green B) x 1d |\n2 - 6 |\nFertile Soil (300G/Green A) |\n7+ |\nAbundant Soil (2,000G/Green S) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Green Cemetery","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"1fdW3p5uu33ciIQf","name":"Abyss Tree","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:abyss-tree","level":13,"monsterType":"Plant","intelligence":"Low","perception":"Magic","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":0,"languages":"Arcana, Daemonic","habitat":"Abyss","reputation":20,"weakness":23,"weakPoint":"Fire damage +3 points","initiative":19,"movementSpeed":"-","fortitude":"17 (24)","willpower":"16 (23)","source":"CR III p. 359","description":"This tree can be found in Shallow Abyss. It does not look much different from other trees and is difficult to distinguish from a distance.\n\nHowever, it acts with its own will, including casting spells. Its purpose is to maintain the Shallow Abyss in which it lives.\n\nTherefore, it cooperates with monsters protecting Shallow Abyss and takes measures such as sharing HP. Because of its ability to share, it is necessary to find and defeat this tree before clearing the Shallow Abyss.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"► Spiritualism Magic 12 Level/Magic Power 14 (21)","description":""},{"title":"◯ 🗨 ► Magic Aptitude","description":"They can use the Combat Feats [ Multi-Action ], [ Targeting ], [ Magic Convergence ], [ Magic Control ], [ Hawk Eye ], [ Universal Metamagic ], [ Rune Master ], and [ Wordbreak ]."},{"title":"◯ Abyss Connection","description":"When this monster is in Shallow Abyss, it may share HP with a monster existing in the same Shallow Abyss. In this case, as long as the target monster exists in the Shallow Abyss, it can choose to receive the applied damage to its HP as fixed damage that would otherwise be dealt to the Trunk section. The distance from the target is not taken into account, and it is not necessary to be visible. Any number of monsters can be the target of this effect.\nThe HP of the target cannot be used to heal the damage already suffered by the Trunk section."},{"title":"◯ Regeneration = 9 points","description":"At the end of each round, the Abyss Tree recovers 9 HP. This has no effect if the Abyss Tree has 0 HP or lower.\nBranch"},{"title":"◯ Attack Obstacle = +4 • +4","description":"The tree's giant body hinders attacks.\nThe Trunk section gains a +4 bonus to Evasion checks against melee and ranged attacks.\nThis effect disappears when any Branch section falls to 0 HP or lower."},{"title":"► Toxic Branch/15 (22)/Willpower/Negates","description":"A Branch strikes \"Target: 1 Character\" with the Abyss branch and leaves within \"Range: Touch.\"\nThe target suffers 2d+15 magic damage and, at the same time, randomly loses one of its items if it has any of the following items in its inventory: herbs, potions, or medicine. This effect is a Curse type.\nOn the turn when any Branch section uses this ability, other Branch sections cannot use this ability.\n2d |\nLoot |\nAlways |\nAbyss Tree Branches (1,900G/Green S) |\n2 - 9 |\nAbyss Tree Leaves (300G/Green A) x 1d |\n10+ |\nAbyss Tree Black Leaves (4,000G/Green S) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Abyss Tree","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"2Ol1esKNQ21KO6Bw","name":"Grown Dracaena Tree","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:grown-dracaena-tree","level":7,"monsterType":"Plant","intelligence":"Average","perception":"Magic","disposition":"Neutral","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Forests, Caves","reputation":15,"weakness":18,"weakPoint":"Fire damage +3 points","initiative":14,"movementSpeed":"13","fortitude":"10 (17)","willpower":"9 (16)","source":"Ancient Blue (SW2.5 supplement) p. 136","description":"The Grown Dracaena Tree is an elder of the Dracaena Trees who, through long years, has gained self-awareness and intellect. It uses nature magic and nurtures all forest plants and creatures, including the Dracaena Trees, as if they were its own children.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯Dragon Mimicry / 8 (15) / Detect Check","description":"Mimics the form of a dragon. Even if a Monster Knowledge check is performed against this monster, it will be identified as a Draconet .\nIf a Detect check against Target Number 15 is performed on this monster and succeeds, you recognize that it is not a Draconet and can perform a normal Monster Knowledge check.\nBody"},{"title":"►Seed Burst / 8 (15) / Fortitude / Half","description":"From the part mimicking a dragon's mouth, it forcefully launches seeds that explode. Using \"Range/Area: 1 (10m) / Shot ,\" deals 2d+6 points of Bludgeoning magic damage to targets in \"1 area (4m radius) / 10\".\nThis ability cannot be used in consecutive turns."},{"title":"► Nature Magic 7 Level / Magic Power 10 (17)","description":""},{"title":"◯🗨Magic Aptitude","description":"They can use the Combat Feats [ Targeting ], [ Metamagic/Targets ], and [ Multi-Action ].\nWing"},{"title":"🗨Power Strike I","description":"Increases damage by +4 points. As a risk, the declared section receives a -2 penalty to Evasion checks.\n2d |\nLoot |\n2 - 8 |\nExploded Seed Fragments (150G/Green A) x 2d |\n9+ |\nExplosive Seed (1,400/Green S) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Grown Dracaena Tree","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"2aK80yzYp5HeWwAK","name":"Marionette Ivy","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:marionette-ivy","level":8,"monsterType":"Plant","intelligence":"None","perception":"Magic","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Forests, Swamps","reputation":15,"weakness":18,"weakPoint":"Fire Damage +3","initiative":14,"movementSpeed":"10 (Dependence)/-","fortitude":"12 (19)","willpower":"11 (18)","source":"BM","description":"A parasitic, mobile plant whose ivy is usually tangled around the carcass of an animal. At first glance, it looks as if the tentacle and flowers are growing out of a moving corpse, and as a result, it is sometimes confused with the undead. However, this corpse is simply a corpse, and the plant that it is moving it about is the real body.\n\nIt wanders through forests and swamps in search of its next host. They are overly aggressive and attack by entangling and otherwise blocking movement.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Psychic Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯ 2 Actions","description":"Marionette Ivy can perform two Major Actions in one round."},{"title":"► Snaring Vines / 12 (19) / Fortitude / Negates","description":"The Marionette Ivy can use its Vine to ensnare a target within \"Range: Touch\" and \"Target: 1 Character\". If the target fails to resist, they are ensnared, unable to move, and receive a -4 penalty to Evasion checks. This effect is not cumulative. When the target tries to escape, use de-bonding (see ML, p. 71).\nBecause of its countless number of vines, Marionette Ivy can attack or use [ ► Snaring Vines] even if it is already ensnared another target.\n2d |\nLoot |\nAlways |\nMagical Vine (80G / Green B) x 1d |\n2 - 11 |\nNothing |\n12+ |\nRemains of the Dead (500G / White A) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Marionette Ivy","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"55BbgS4wLJg1LPrE","name":"Bloody Petal","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:bloody-petal","level":5,"monsterType":"Plant","intelligence":"None","perception":"Magic","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Forests","reputation":11,"weakness":14,"weakPoint":"Fire damage + 3 points","initiative":10,"movementSpeed":"5 (Many Legs)","fortitude":"11 (18)","willpower":"9 (16)","source":"CR I p. 415","description":"Plants with large petals as red as blood, these root-less plants will chase prey down, albeit slowly. Also referred to as \"flesh-eating flowers,\" these plants will capture both animals and Humanoids alike, slowly dissolving their prey for nutrition.\n\nIf the flower is in full bloom and fed a healthy amount of blood, the petals of the plant can be distilled into quality medicine. Rarely a few fruits of the bloody petal can be found as well.\n\nThis monster has only one Trunk but has 3 to 5 Petals. The GM can use 2 + (half of 1d) to randomly determine the amount of Petals, if necessary.\n\nHoodlings like to feed Humanoids to these flowers and may lure them in by pretending to flee.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Regeneration = 5 points","description":"At the end of each round, the Body and all remaining Petal sections recover 5 HP.\nIf a Petal has 0 or less HP, this effect ends on that petal. If the Body has 0 or less HP, this effect disappears for the entire creature.\nPetal"},{"title":"◯ Paralysis Poison/7 (14)/Fortitude/Negates","description":"If a Petal attack hits, the target suffers a -1 penalty to Accuracy and Evasion check for 10 seconds (1 round). This effect is not cumulative.\nThis effect is of the Poison type.\n2d |\nLoot |\nAlways |\nCrimson Petals (120G/Green A) |\n2 - 8 |\nNothing |\n9+ |\nRed Berries (300G/Green A) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Bloody Petal","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"7DNTrjTg8wTkp7sK","name":"Campanella Spruce","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:campanella-spruce","level":7,"monsterType":"Plant","intelligence":"Low","perception":"Magic","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":0,"languages":"","habitat":"Forests, Shallows","reputation":13,"weakness":17,"weakPoint":"Fire damage +3 points","initiative":12,"movementSpeed":"9","fortitude":"10 (17)","willpower":"9 (16)","source":"Natural History of Ursyla p. 128","description":"In the dark depths of the Great Sebrae Forest stands a black-barked tree that moves independently. At the ends of its distinctively drooping branches hang bell-shaped fruits that emit a bluish-white glow. These fruits pulse with a unique rhythm, exerting a hypnotic effect that draws creatures toward them.\n\nAfter gathering living beings this way, the tree causes its impact-sensitive fruits to burst, releasing a powerful poisonous gas that indiscriminately infects its victims. All the corpses become nutrients for the Campanella Spruce, which then bears new fruits whose beautiful colors correspond to the nutrients absorbed.\n\nWhile this species was originally brought from the Abyss, it seems to thrive and disrupt the ecosystem in Sebrae, perhaps due to the land's rich magic. As a result, adventurers receive constant requests to cut these trees down. The harvested bell-shaped fruits are highly sought after by certain \"unhinged\" researchers.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Limited 2 Actions","description":"It can perform 2 Major Actions in 1 round. However, [►Flickering Bell] can only be used once per round at most."},{"title":"►Flickering Bell / 9 (16) / Willpower / Negates","description":"Causes the fruit to flash and emit light, creating a hypnotic effect in \"Range: Caster\" and \"Target: all areas (Radius 30m) / All.\" Characters who fail their Willpower check must move as close as possible to this monster during their turn using Normal Move. They cannot perform any Major Actions or Minor Actions, and their turn ends.\nThis effect is Psychic (Weak) type and only lasts for 10 seconds (1 round). Characters with \"Perception: Magic\" or those who are closing their eyes or in a blind state are not affected by this effect."},{"title":"►Quietly Breaking Bell / 9 (16) / Fortitude / Half","description":"This effect can only be used when the user's current HP is at or below half (rounded up) of their maximum HP. One of the fruits bursts, spraying a highly corrosive liquid in \"Range: Caster\" \"Target: 1 area (radius 4m) / 10,\" dealing 2d+4 points of magic damage.\nUsing this effect causes the user to take 5 points of fixed damage to their HP."},{"title":"◯ Delicate Loot","description":"The quantity of loot Bell Fruit is reduced by the number of times this monster used [►Quietly Breaking Bell] during combat (minimum 0).\n2d |\nLoot |\nAlways |\nBell Fruit (90G/Green B) x 6 |\n2 - 6 |\nBark (50G/Green B) |\n7+ |\nBlack Bark (400G/Green A) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Campanella Spruce","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"7u26TxqwmRvBS4Nz","name":"Daemonwood","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:daemonwood","level":14,"monsterType":"Plant","intelligence":"Average","perception":"Magic","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Forest","reputation":18,"weakness":22,"weakPoint":"Fire damage +3 points","initiative":19,"movementSpeed":"10 (Many Legs)","fortitude":"17 (24)","willpower":"16 (23)","source":"Monstrous Lore p. 130","description":"This is one of the Living Tree species, which walks using its roots as legs. It has an eerily twisted, humped trunk with countless thin branches.\n\nThis evil plant does not use leaves, but has excellent mental sensitivity and communicates its will to others in a kind of telepathy. The weak- minded are overwhelmed by it and become unable to act.\n\nThis tree communicates with the Otherworld, and Daemons can be summoned by opening the Abyss Gate. Scholars suspect, from its bizarre appearance, that it may be a creature that has been modified by the Otherworld Daemons to invade this world.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"► Open Abyss Gate","description":"Opens an Abyss Gate and summons a Daemon , just as a Daemonologist does. Only Daemons with monster level 13 or lower can be summoned. When a Daemonwood uses this ability, it spends \"Monster level x 2\" points of MP for the Daemon it summons. This ability cannot be used if a Daemon has already been summoned by this tree.\nThe summoned Daemon acts according to the Daemon Action Chart (see ML p. 46), but if the roll is 1, the Daemon is sent away without doing anything (this monster does need to spend MP for canceling its action).\nWhen a new Daemon is invoked after the Daemon is returned, it cannot be the same Daemon as the one that was summoned immediately before. It must be a different type from the previous one.\nWhen this monster is defeated, the summoned Daemon is automatically sent back, and the Abyss Gate that was created disappears."},{"title":"⏩ Oppressive Will/18 (25)/Willpower/Negates","description":"Within \"Range/Area: 2 (30m) / Target ,\" pressurize the spirit of the \"Target: 1 Entire Character\" with its own thoughts.\nA target who fails a resistance receives a -2 penalty to any action check for the next 3 minutes (18 rounds).\nThis effect is of a Psychic type and is cumulative without an upper limit.\nThis ability may be used up to three times per round but may not be used more than once on the same enemy in the same round.\n2d |\nLoot |\nAlways |\nAbyss Tree Leaves (300G/Green A) x 2d |\n2 - 8 |\nGray Bark (400G/Green A) x 1d |\n9+ |\nMagic Bark (4,000G/Gold Green S) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Daemonwood","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"8JRGBsm2vRfddXLY","name":"Lake Balloon","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:lake-balloon","level":4,"monsterType":"Plant","intelligence":"None","perception":"Magic","disposition":"Neutral","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Lakesides","reputation":11,"weakness":14,"weakPoint":"Fire damage +3","initiative":10,"movementSpeed":"10 (Swimming &amp; Floating)","fortitude":"6 (13)","willpower":"6 (13)","source":"Natural History of Dorden p. 125","description":"This plant is formed by a spherical algae about 2 meters in diameter that can be seen in Great Luana Lake surrounding Orphid Lake Country in the Dorden region. It mainly lives underwater, but can also be seen floating on the surface of the lake.\n\nThe interior of the spherical body is hollow and serves as a dwelling for Fairies . When underwater, it houses water fairies, and when floating, it houses wind fairies.\n\nIt is rumored that mana becomes active and unstable around this monster.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯Underwater Aptitude","description":"There are no restrictions or penalties for actions in water."},{"title":"►Mana Activation","description":"Activates the surrounding mana, causing magical and other effects to become stronger and more unstable.\nFor 10 seconds (1 round), all MP consumption for characters within a “Radius of 30m (all areas)/All” centered on the user increases by 1 point. If the increased MP cannot be consumed, actions requiring that MP consumption cannot be performed.\nAlso, any Spellcasting check treats a roll of 3 as an \"automatic failure\" and a roll of 11 as an \"automatic success\".\nUsing this effect consumes 8 MP.\nThis ability is used preferentially over other actions when the Lake Balloon is able to use it."},{"title":"◯Fairy's Grace","description":"Characters classified as \"fairy\" (including Fey ) within a radius of 30m (all areas) / All, centered on Lake Balloon, recover 1d points of HP and MP at the end of the target's turn."},{"title":"◯Delicate Loot","description":"If the Balloon's HP falls to 0 or less while the unique skill [►Mana Activation] is in effect, all \"Mana-infused Algae\" loot is lost.\n2d |\nLoot |\nAlways |\nMana-infused Algae (100G/Green a) x 1d |\n2 - 8 |\nNothing |\n9+ |\nMysterious Seeds (100G/Green A) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Lake Balloon","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"9GB5TTGIHF3XlCBJ","name":"Coiled Ivy","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:coiled-ivy","level":4,"monsterType":"Plant","intelligence":"None","perception":"Magic","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Forests, Swamps","reputation":11,"weakness":14,"weakPoint":"Fire damage +3 points","initiative":11,"movementSpeed":"10(leap)","fortitude":"6 (13)","willpower":"5 (12)","source":"VC","description":"The monster is a spiral-shaped, thick vine. It moves by leaping and expanding itself like a spring. It usually wraps around the trunks of other large trees and is considered a threat on offense. It can convert its elasticity into striking power.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Elasticity","description":"On a successful Evasion check against melee attacks, the Coiled Ivy gains +3 damage points on its next turn. This effect is not cumulative.\n2d |\nLoot |\n2 - 6 |\nNothing |\n7+ |\nElastic Vines (120G/Green A) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Coiled Ivy","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"9fo6ycuucvbEiomz","name":"Meria Mistletoe","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:meria-mistletoe","level":6,"monsterType":"Plant","intelligence":"None","perception":"Magic","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Forest","reputation":13,"weakness":16,"weakPoint":"Accuracy +1","initiative":13,"movementSpeed":"10 (Crawling)","fortitude":"9 (16)","willpower":"9 (16)","source":"CR II p. 365","description":"This is a plant that parasitizes other species and absorbs nutrients from them. It looks like a clump of sand daisies and usually crawls on the ground.\n\nIt is characterized by its ability to frequently change parasite hosts. It generally parasitizes plants, but occasionally it parasitizes Humanoids, Barbarous, and animals. Among Humanoids, the parasite often targets and parasitizes Meria or Arbors , probably because of their origins.\n\nIt is dangerous to encounter it alone, as it's a parasite that can quickly take the life of its host. Since they do not attack Constructs, Conjurers are very useful for their cleanup.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Nutrients Consumption","description":"If a character of the Meria or Arbor race is the target of a melee attack, it is preferentially selected as the target. On the other hand, a character with [ ◯ Poison Immunity] will not be chosen as a target."},{"title":"◯ Implantation/8 (15)/Willpower/Negates","description":"The target hit by the attack with Ivy is put to sleep, and the target is implanted with a parasite.\nThe target falls asleep on the spot. This sleep is not awakened by the passage of time or by natural means. While asleep, the target's maximum HP is reduced by 1 point every 10 seconds (1 round). If this effect causes the maximum HP to reach 0, the target dies without making a Death Check.\nThis effect is of the Psychic type. It can be removed by the [ Awaken ] spell, [ Early Bird ] spellsong, or other awakening effects, but the success value must be compared. An Awake Potion cannot be used to remove this effect.\n2d |\nLoot |\n2 - 4 |\nMagical Vine (30G/Green B) |\n5 - 11 |\nStrong Vine (300G/Green A) |\n12+ |\nMagical Vine (600G/Gold Green A) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Meria Mistletoe","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"BIET9djtQ59tsPQC","name":"Rock Lotus Tree","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:rock-lotus-tree","level":8,"monsterType":"Plant","intelligence":"None","perception":"Magic","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Plains, Forests, Shallows","reputation":15,"weakness":17,"weakPoint":"Physical damage +2 points","initiative":13,"movementSpeed":"8 (3 Legs)","fortitude":"11 (18)","willpower":"10 (17)","source":"AB, p. 96","description":"This is a tree that walks slowly using its thick roots like legs, reaching a height of 3-4m and a diameter of 7-8m. It is called \"Tree\" because it is covered with stiff bark from near the base to the trunk, reminiscent of a turtle's shell. It contains an Abyss Shard inside its body. The tips of its hemispherically spread branches are covered with countless Rockwool Fluffs .","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯Psychic Immunity","description":"Trunk"},{"title":"🗨Cleave I","description":"It can attack up to 3 characters with melee attacks that can be reached, but the damage will be reduced by -3."},{"title":"⏩Fluff Release","description":"Releases \"1d\" Rockwool Fluff . The released Rockwool Fluff begins acting immediately.\nWhen using this effect, Trunk section takes fixed damage equal to the number of released Rockwool Fluff.\nThis effect can only be used once per turn and cannot be used in consecutive turns."},{"title":"⏩Fluff Detonate","description":"Within \"Range: Caster,\" simultaneously reduces the HP of Rockwool Fluff within 2-3 areas (10m radius / All) to \"0.\"\nIn resolving individual [◯Fluff Burst] effects triggered by this, other Rockwool Fluff whose HP was reduced to 0 simultaneously cannot become targets of this ability (meaning no double triggering).\nThis monster's own Trunk and Root sections can become targets (though they don't take damage).\nRoot"},{"title":"◯Attack Obstacle =+4 • None","description":"Size hinders attacks.\nTrunk section gains a +4 bonus to Evasion checks against melee attacks. This effect is lost when 2 or more Root sections have 0 or less HP."},{"title":"◯Painful Strike","description":"If the result of 2d for damage determination is 10 or higher, increase the damage by an additional +8 points.\n2d |\nLoot |\nAlways |\nAbyss Shard (200G/-) |\n2 - 7 |\nWood (150G/Green A) |\n8 - 11 |\nHard Wood (300G/Green A) |\n12+ |\nSuper Hard Wood (900G/Green Black A) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Rock Lotus Tree","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"BqkTNRsvM6xn6S2E","name":"Giant Fluffball","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:giant-fluffball","level":8,"monsterType":"Plant","intelligence":"None","perception":"Magic","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Wilderness","reputation":14,"weakness":17,"weakPoint":"Fire damage +3 points","initiative":14,"movementSpeed":"-/15(Floating)","fortitude":"11 (18)","willpower":"10 (17)","source":"CR III p. 356","description":"Found throughout the continent of Alframe in wastelands with little fruitfulness, this is a huge mass of cottony hairs up to 3 meters in length. They are sometimes seen floating in the wind.\n\nIt attacks any creature that comes near it and plants hairs on its body. The hairs absorb the host's life force and sprout as a seedbed.\n\nThey are called \"Deadly Fluff\" by merchants, travelers, and adventurers, who are told to stay away from them and run away if they see them.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Fluff Body","description":"The monster does not receive a critical hit from blunt weapons and is treated as having a Defense value of 3 points higher against blunt weapons."},{"title":"◯ Fire Vulnerability","description":"When the Giant Fluffball is hit by Fire-type damage, it takes an extra 3 damage."},{"title":"◯ Fluff Scatter/Can't","description":"If the target character (a character who is hit by a Slam or a character who hits this monster with a melee attack) automatically gains 1 \"fluff point\". This effect accumulates until the number of \"fluff points\" reaches 5."},{"title":"◯ Fluff Explosion/Can't","description":"The Fluff section explodes and scatters cotton wool within \"Range: Caster\" when its HP becomes 0. In \"Target: 1 area (5m Radius)/15,\" gets 1d x \"fluff points.\" Fluff points are accumulated until the number of points reaches 5 for each target.\nAfter this effect occurs, the Fluff section automatically fails the Death Check."},{"title":"◯ Fluff Disease/11 (18)/Fortitude/Negates","description":"A character with 1 or more \"fluff points\" receives \"fluff points\" of fixed damage at the end of their turn. This effect is a disease type and lasts for 1 day.\nA character can pull out the fluff from \"Target: 1 Character\" (including itself) within \"Range: Touch\" with a Major Action. This makes the target's \"fluff points\" automatically reduced by -1.\n2d |\nLoot |\n2 - 10 |\nDangerous Fluff (200G/Green A) |\n11+ |\nAsh Fluff (2,000G/Green S) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Giant Fluffball","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"D4jk3bjA1jMfBI67","name":"Yggdrasil Sapling","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:yggdrasil-sapling","level":20,"monsterType":"Plant","intelligence":"High","perception":"Magic","disposition":"Neutral","soulscars":0,"languages":"Sylvan","habitat":"Forests","reputation":18,"weakness":23,"weakPoint":"Fire damage +3 points","initiative":20,"movementSpeed":"-","fortitude":"26 (33)","willpower":"27 (34)","source":"CR III p. 361","description":"In Raxia, the name \"Yggdrasil\" is the name of the great World Tree, the largest tree known to humanity, which has been rooted in Raxia since the beginning of the Divine Civilization. This young tree is but a sapling of another Yggdrasil, resulting from a seed flung far from the original tree that has taken root. Though it is young compared to the original World Tree, the Yggdrasil Sapling is still large enough to scrape the heavens and cannot be accurately measured using current equipment. It is said that the history of Raxia lies engraved in its leaves and branches, and those who can find even a fallen twig of the tree can find themselves with a wealth of knowledge.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Water/Ice Immunity, ◯ Earth Immunity","description":"Trunk"},{"title":"◯ 3 Actions","description":"The Trunk can perform three Major Actions in one round."},{"title":"► Fairy Magic 15 Level/Magic Power 27 (34)","description":"Can use Earth, Water/Ice, Light, and Dark types."},{"title":"◯ 🗨 ► Magic Aptitude","description":"They can use the Combat Feats [ Targeting ], [ Magic Convergence ], [ Magic Control ], [ Hawk Eye ], [ Universal Metamagic ], [ Double Cast ], [ Rune Master ], and [ Wordbreak ]."},{"title":"◯ Breath of the World Tree","description":"The Yggdrasil Sapling brings the vitality of nature into its body. At the end of each round, the Trunk sections recover 20 HP and MP.\nThis effect is lost if the HP of the Trunk section becomes 0 or less.\nBranch"},{"title":"◯ Long Branches","description":"An attack on a branch can be made within \"Range/Area: 2 (20m) / Target \"."},{"title":"◯ Branch Cover","description":"If the Yggdrasil Sapling's Trunk is attacked by a melee or ranged attack, a spell with \"Area: Shot \" with \"Target: 1 Character\", a Branch may move in the way of the attack, taking the damage instead automatically (no Evasion, Fortitude, or Willpower check needed). The branch cannot reduce damage with its defense or other effects.\nEach Branch may only do this once per round. This unique skill is automatically used when the trunk is attacked, but GM should decide which Branch will take the hit.\nThis does not protect the Trunk from \"Area: Target \" spells or wide-area effects."},{"title":"► Branch Dance/Can't","description":"The Yggdrasil Sapling deals (2d x (Remaining Branches) + 5) Physical damage to one target in the same skirmish.\nThis ability cannot be used if even one Branch has completed its Major Action. Also, after using this ability, the Major Actions of all Branches are completed.\n2d |\nLoot |\nAlways |\nYggdrasil Leaf (5,000G/Green S) |\n2 - 6 |\nNothing |\n7 - 12 |\nYggdrasil Branch (15,000G/Green SS) |\n13+ |\nGreat Yggdrasil Branch (40,000G/Green SS) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Yggdrasil Sapling","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"EdP2C8dKYHeuGq6d","name":"Steam Pod","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:steam-pod","level":2,"monsterType":"Plant","intelligence":"None","perception":"Magic","disposition":"Neutral","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Forest","reputation":7,"weakness":11,"weakPoint":"Lightning damage + 3 points","initiative":7,"movementSpeed":"5 (Creeping)","fortitude":"4 (11)","willpower":"3 (10)","source":"CR I p. 414","description":"This is a plant about 3 meters across, with a large fleshy sac shaped vaguely like a saddle. It has numerous long and short vines to strike down approaching animals or pull itself by crawling on the ground or in trees.\n\nIt constantly expels the steam that builds up in its sac, keeping the surroundings hot and humid, which they prefer. This environment is unpleasant for most organisms but desirable for a limited number of livestock breeders and farmers, and the seeds are sold at high prices.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Unpleasant Vapor/Can't","description":"At \"Range: Self\" and \"Target: 1 area (5m radius) / Space,\" the Steam Pod creates an unpleasant environment for the creatures by blowing steam.\nAny character within range receives a -1 penalty to all Accuracy and Evasion checks. This effect is a poison effect.\nMonsters whose Habitat includes \"Forests,\" \"Marshes,\" or \"Caves\" are not affected by this effect.\n2d |\nLoot |\nAlways |\nSteam Distillation (30G/Green B) |\n2 - 10 |\nNothing |\n11+ |\nSteam Vine Seeds (120G/Green A) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Steam Pod","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"FM98gVKw0QDkvRCp","name":"Alraune","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:alraune","level":1,"monsterType":"Plant","intelligence":"Low","perception":"Five Senses","disposition":"Neutral","soulscars":0,"languages":"Trade Common","habitat":"Plains, Forests","reputation":9,"weakness":12,"weakPoint":"Physical Damage +2","initiative":7,"movementSpeed":"10/-","fortitude":"2 (9)","willpower":"4 (11)","source":"Battle Mastery p. 123","description":"Alraunes are plant monsters that look like small children, around 80cm tall, with large white flowers blooming out of their heads. Very timid, they will attempt to escape immediately when startled, but are curious and will watch from a distance if possible. Alraunes have a child-like personality, and if treated appropriately can be made to be fond of humans.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"► Piercing Scream/3 (10)/Willpower/Negates","description":"The Alraune lets out a high-pitched scream and stuns \"Target: All Area (20m Radius)/All\" within \"Range: Caster.\" This effect is treated as a Psychic (Weak) type.\nThe target will fall prone as soon as it is stunned.\n2d |\nLoot |\n2 - 8 |\nNothing |\n9+ |\nMysterious Seeds (100G / Green A) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Alraune","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"FaHn4xPxh1Q3FrHA","name":"Spring Ivy","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:spring-ivy","level":5,"monsterType":"Plant","intelligence":"None","perception":"Magic","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Forests","reputation":12,"weakness":15,"weakPoint":"Fire damage +3 points","initiative":12,"movementSpeed":"10 (Jump)","fortitude":"7 (14)","willpower":"6 (13)","source":"Natural History of Burlight p. 123","description":"This creature can be found in forests throughout the Burlight Region. It is a vine monster that typically coils itself around large trees. When something larger than a small animal comes within 10 meters, it breaks free and attacks, attempting to strangle its prey with snaring vines. This instinctive \"hunting\" behavior enables the creature to acquire nutrients and grow.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯Psychic Immunity","description":""},{"title":"🗨Bouncing","description":"This effect can be declared only if its own Accuracy check was successful in the previous turn, and can be declared anytime during turn.\nWithin Range: 1 (10m), a character (section) other than the one that had hit the target before is randomly selected, and a Snaring Vines attack is made against it. In an attack with this effect, the monster moves to the target location (Simplified Combat: area, Standard/Advanced Combat: coordinates), regardless of whether the Accuracy check is successful or not. Movement restrictions by skirmish area are not taken into account, and its movement cannot be blocked. In Standard Combat (even in Advanced Combat), for position determination when the attack target is affected by the [ Cover II ] effect, please refer to page 66 of the Core Rulebook II.\n2d |\nLoot |\n2 - 4 |\nNothing |\n5 - 7 |\nMagical Vine (30G/Green B) |\n8+ |\nMighty Vine (300G/Green A) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Spring Ivy","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"FmcTQQqxuMNGFiEa","name":"Moldsaurus","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:moldsaurus","level":10,"monsterType":"Plant","intelligence":"None","perception":"Magic","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Swamps, Forests, Shallows","reputation":16,"weakness":21,"weakPoint":"Fire damage +3 points","initiative":17,"movementSpeed":"11","fortitude":"14 (21)","willpower":"12 (19)","source":"AB, p. 96","description":"This is a saurid-shaped mold colony that has grown gigantic and become mobile after absorbing an Abyss Shard. Sightings are heavily concentrated in Shallow Abysses, with almost no cases of discovery outside of a Shallows.\n\nIt appears as a massive bipedal carnivorous dinosaur, 8-10 meters in total length, with a vivid purple back and yellow-green belly. Upon closer inspection, it would appear unnatural for a reptile or dinosaur due to its lack of eyes, sticky body surface, and immobile parts that resemble forelimbs.\n\nIt engulfs virtually any living thing as nutrients. It primarily swallows prey through a mouth-like section to store them inside its body, but given enough time, it can also absorb them through its body surface by extending fungal filaments. Though its movements are sluggish, it has no bones or vital organs, and possesses excellent flexibility and durability.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯Soft Body","description":"When receiving damage from blunt weapons, Defense is treated as 5 points higher. Cannot be targeted by Throw or similar attack methods."},{"title":"◯Regeneration = 5(10) points","description":"At the end of the turn, all sections recover 5 HP. Sections with 0 or less HP do not recover.\nWithin a Shallow Abyss, this recovery amount becomes 10 points.\nUpper Body"},{"title":"►Poisonous Gas Breath / 12 (19) / Fortitude / Half","description":"With \"Range/Area: 20m / Shot \", exhales poison gas at \"Target: 1 area (4m radius) / 10\", dealing 2d+10 Poison magic damage.\nThis ability cannot be used in consecutive turns.\nLower Body"},{"title":"◯Attack Obstacle =+4 • None","description":"Size hinders attacks.\nThe Upper Body section gains a +4 bonus to Evasion checks against melee attacks. This effect is lost when the Lower Body section has 0 or less HP."},{"title":"🗨Tail Sweep","description":"The monster can use its tail to attack up to 5 targets in the same skirmish. This attack cannot be used in consecutive rounds.\n2d |\nLoot |\nAlways |\nAbyss Shard (200G/-) |\n2 - 8 |\nNothing |\n9 - 12 |\nFlesh Ganoderma (1,000G/Green S) |\n13+ |\nBig Flesh Ganoderma (5,000G/Green S) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Moldsaurus","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"Mp6agm5O9tYx1sKS","name":"Belladonna","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:belladonna","level":12,"monsterType":"Plant","intelligence":"None","perception":"Magic","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Forests, Meadow","reputation":16,"weakness":20,"weakPoint":"Fire damage +3 points","initiative":12,"movementSpeed":"15","fortitude":"16 (23)","willpower":"14 (21)","source":"CR III p. 358","description":"A Belladonna appears at first glance to be a green-skinned Humanoid, but upon closer investigation is actually a plant whose vines have been so entwined with each other they can take the shape of a human. By taking a humanoid shape, the Belladonna can move much more easily to attack prey and will drain nutrients from anything it has killed, animal or otherwise. It will also hide in forests, using its plant body to disguise itself before surprising prey.\n\nThe vines of a Belladonna contain a horrific poison, causing high fevers, nausea, and even death from just a touch. However, the leaves from the Belladonna's vines can be turned into an antidote for this contact poison, so it is recommended to slay the Belladonna before the poison spreads throughout the victim's body.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Psychic Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯ Persistent Poison/16 (23)/Fortitude/Negates","description":"If the Belladonna melee attack hits, the target will be poisoned.\nA character affected by poison immediately suffers 2d Poison magic damage and continues to suffer similar damage every hour (without Fortitude checks). This effect persists unless the poison is removed, but it is not cumulative.\nThe Belladonna Leaves characters can get when they kill this monster contains a counterpoison that can remove the effects of this poison without contested checks. One leaf can heal 1 person.\nUpper Body"},{"title":"► Snaring Vines/14 (21)/Fortitude/Negates","description":"As a Major Action, the Belladonna can use its Vine to ensnare a target in the same skirmish. If the target fails to resist, they are ensnared, unable to move, and receive a -4 penalty to Evasion checks.\nWhen the target tries to escape, use the de-bonding rules.\nThe monster has a large number of vines, and even if it has already entangled a character with [ ► Snaring Vines], it can still make a Melee Attack or a new [ ► Snaring Vines], regardless of the number of vines, even if it has already entangled a character with [ ► Snaring Vines].\n2d |\nLoot |\nAlways |\nBelladonna Leaves (150G/Green A) x 1d |\n2 - 8 |\nNothing |\n9+ |\nPoisonous Flower (500G/Green A) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Belladonna","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"NQISS9v5tuxnK04J","name":"Medusa Head","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:medusa-head","level":9,"monsterType":"Plant","intelligence":"None","perception":"Magic","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Rivers, Lakes, Seas","reputation":16,"weakness":19,"weakPoint":"Bludgeoning Damage +3","initiative":14,"movementSpeed":"-/10 (Swimming)","fortitude":"13(20)","willpower":"10(17)","source":"BM","description":"Drifting in the water, this dangerous seaweed gets its name from the fact that it looks at first glance like the head of a medusa, with snakelike hair flowing.\n\nThe part that looks like the hair is a transformed root originally intended to stick to rocks and other objects. The roots are covered with numerous fine thorns, which petrify the victim of their wounds. This ability is one of the reasons for its name.\n\nMedusa Heads often drift through the water in groups and attack their prey. They then sink to the seafloor with their petrified prey, gradually chipping away at their poor, stoned victims for sustenance.\n\nThis fearsome seaweed is found mainly in the ocean, but there are also subspecies present in freshwater and rarely in rivers and lakes, where it is intentionally cultivated by Gilman and Mermen to protect their territories. In such cases, they are roped and wired together to prevent them from becoming adrift.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Underwater","description":"The Medusa Head doesn't receive penalties for moving or taking Action in water. However, it can't perform any Action without water."},{"title":"◯ 2 Actions","description":"Medusa Head can perform two Major Actions in one round."},{"title":"◯ Counter","description":"A Medusa Head can use [ Counter ] Combat Feat."},{"title":"◯ Petrifying Tentacle / 12 (19) / Fortitude / Negates","description":"If a tentacle attack hits and this Resistance Check fails, the target becomes Petrified (Agility – 12).\nThis effect is Poison type.\n2d |\nLoot |\nAlways |\nSlimy Tentacles (300G / Green A) |\n2 - 7 |\nPetrifying Poison Gland (100G / Green A) |\n8 - 11 |\nDeadly Petrifying Poison Gland (500G / Green A) |\n12+ |\nPetrifying Poison Crystal (200G / Green S) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Medusa Head","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"P1zugXJYhkZpYQSB","name":"Fungal Parasite","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:fungal-parasite","level":11,"monsterType":"Plant","intelligence":"Low","perception":"Magic","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":0,"languages":"Trade Common","habitat":"Forests, Caves, Ruins","reputation":19,"weakness":22,"weakPoint":"Fire damage + 3 points","initiative":15,"movementSpeed":"12","fortitude":"14 (21)","willpower":"13 (20)","source":"CR II p. 368","description":"This monster is a humanoid covered in parasitic mushrooms, feeding the mushroom as it decomposes. Typically found in dark, damp places, the Fungal Parasite will attack any humanoid or animal passing by, hoping to infect them and use them as a new host. Fungal Parasite hosts will last for a year or two before becoming desiccated husks, drained of all vital nutrients.\n\nIt is possible to save a victim of the Fungal Parasites, though it involves casting a [ Refresh ] spell on a host whose HP has been reduced to 0.\n\nRarely, a mushroom called \"Forest Marvel\" may grow among the various Fungal Parasites. This mushroom is non-toxic and quite delicious, so it is valued by many in the culinary community. Additionally, it is thought to have anti-aging properties, and some elder priests have sent out adventurers to look for these mushrooms.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"⏩ Sporulation/11 (18)/Fortitude/Negates","description":"This unique skill can be used only once per round.\nThe Fungal Parasite spreads reddish-purple spores in \"Range: Caster\" and \"Target: 1 area (6m Radius) / 20\", infecting the target with a disease called sporotrichosis . This effect is treated as a Disease type.\nCharacter infected with sporotrichosis will have small reddish-purple mushrooms sprouting from all over their body after 1 day, and their all ability scores will be reduced by -6 points. Fixed characters suffer a -1 penalty to Accuracy, Evasion, Fortitude, and Willpower.\nIf any ability scores reach 0 or 3 full days have passed since the spore infection, the character will fall into a severe hallucinatory state and cannot act at all. The character in this state will spread spores every round, regardless of their will.\nAfter a few days of infection, the characters will be lost entirely, and the character becomes a Fungal Parasite. If the character has fallen into this state, it cannot be recovered by effects that heal disease, such as [ Cure Disease ]."},{"title":"► Hallucinogenic Spores/13 (20)/Fortitude/Negates","description":"These blue-violet spores are scattered around the Fungal Parasite, and all those in the same skirmish must make a Fortitude check. Those who fail will see the Fungal Parasite as someone close to them and will move to protect it from anything and anyone who wishes to do it harm (and will do nothing else). Even if the Fungal Parasite attacks an affected character, it will remain under the effect of these spores.\nThis effect is treated as a Disease type.\n2d |\nLoot |\nAlways |\nWilted Mushrooms (30G/Green B) |\n2 - 7 |\nNothing |\n8 - 10 |\nForest Marvel (2,000G/Green S) |\n11+ |\nForest Marvel (2,000G/Green S) x 3 |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Fungal Parasite","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"QcmhROjlFuZkkbfx","name":"Stepping Leaf","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:stepping-leaf","level":4,"monsterType":"Plant","intelligence":"None","perception":"Magic","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Rivers, Ponds","reputation":11,"weakness":14,"weakPoint":"Physical damage +2 points","initiative":10,"movementSpeed":"-/5 (Swimming)","fortitude":"6 (13)","willpower":"5 (12)","source":"CR II p. 364","description":"This is a floating plant that floats on the surface of shallow rivers and ponds, with its round leaves ranging from 30 to 50 cm in diameter. If animals step on them unnoticed, they will drop them into the water and attack them.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Underwater Aptitude","description":""},{"title":"◯ Mimicry/13/Danger Sense/Negates","description":"It can retract its body and mimic a stone. While mimicking, characters cannot perform a Monster Knowledge check on this monster.\nIf a character approaches it unintentionally, they need to make a Danger check with target number 13, and if it fails, they will be surprised (see CR I, p. 144). Mimicry will be automatically ended once the monster starts to act.\nThis monster cannot be detected with [ Sense Magic ].\n2d |\nLoot |\n2 - 5 |\nNothing |\n6 - 8 |\nMagical Vine (30G/Green B) |\n9+ |\nStrong Vine (300G/Green A) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Stepping Leaf","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"S2rwMGfH7SpZ0DTe","name":"Mud Mushroom","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:mud-mushroom","level":3,"monsterType":"Plant","intelligence":"None","perception":"Magic","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Forests, Marshes","reputation":11,"weakness":14,"weakPoint":"Magic damage +2","initiative":9,"movementSpeed":"10","fortitude":"4 (11)","willpower":"4 (11)","source":"Natural History of Dorden p. 125","description":"This is a giant mushroom about 1m long. Short limbs grow from the stem, and its silhouette resembles a human child wearing a cap on its head. It moves its two short legs in quick, small steps, approaching and attacking with body slams. This behavior is not for predation, but rather seems to be a gesture to refuse others entering their habitat.\n\nIt is said that if their ecology were studied in detail, the distribution of their colonies could be determined. However, due to their toughness and large numbers, which exceed their appearance, it is reported that no one is actually studying them.\n\nThe flesh of the mushroom is hard, and it is said to become edible after long simmering. However, the taste is somewhat astringent, and opinions on it are divided.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯Soft Body","description":"Defense against blunt weapons is treated as 3 points higher."},{"title":"◯Delicate Loot","description":"If its HP is reduced to 0 or less by magic damage, the loot item \"Stripe Mushroom\" will be lost.\n2d |\nLoot |\nAlways |\nStripe Mushroom (60G/Green B) |\n2 - 9 |\nNothing |\n10+ |\nSpore Bag (30G/Green B) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Mud Mushroom","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"Spn5goPNrEUFjFBq","name":"Needle Archer","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:needle-archer","level":2,"monsterType":"Plant","intelligence":"None","perception":"Magic","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Forests","reputation":7,"weakness":11,"weakPoint":"Fire damage +3","initiative":4,"movementSpeed":"-/-","fortitude":"4(11)","willpower":"3(10)","source":"BM","description":"This plant is named after the arrow-like needles that grow from it. It shoots these needles at prey that enter its network of vines. The vines are concealed on the forest floor by dirt and dead leaves. Once unsuspecting prey walks into the area, they are violently attacked as the needles are shot at their feet and lower legs.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Psychic Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯ Vine Network","description":"A Needle Archer has thin vines stretching out 2-3 Areas (10m Radius) around itself. If characters don't successfully make a Danger Sense check against Target Number of 12, they will step into it unknowingly and become surprised by Needle Archer.\nIn the event of a Surprise attack, the Needle Archer is placed in the Frontline Area in Simplified Combat. In Standard and Advanced Combat, all PCs are placed within a 10m radius of the monster."},{"title":"◯ Light Needles","description":"The Needle Archer can fire its Needle attack as a ranged attack with Range: 2(20m), though any attacks made at targets outside the [ ◯ Vine Network] receive a -1 penalty to Accuracy."},{"title":"◯ No Blind Spot","description":"Within the [ ◯ Vine Network], Needle Archer can ignore shielding (Standard/Advanced combat) with Needle attacks, and will not suffer Stray Shots if it shoots into the skirmish."},{"title":"🗨 Million Needles","description":"A Needle Archer may attack all characters (enemies and allies) within range of the [ ◯ Vine Network] simultaneously during its turn.\n2d |\nLoot |\nAlways |\nThorn Arrow (150G / Green B) |\n2 - 10 |\nNothing |\n11+ |\nStrong Vine (300G / Green A) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Needle Archer","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"UYfX4kQASCmNmrtG","name":"Gradient Plum","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:gradient-plum","level":6,"monsterType":"Plant","intelligence":"None","perception":"Magic","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Forests","reputation":13,"weakness":16,"weakPoint":"Slashing type damage +3","initiative":13,"movementSpeed":"12(Rotation)","fortitude":"8 (15)","willpower":"8 (15)","source":"VC","description":"This is a large nut, about 1m long. They are soft and moderately teardrop- shaped. When provoked, it sprinkles juice around it to protect itself.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Poison, Disease Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯ Change Color","description":"The color of the whole body changes according to the remaining HP; it turns red when the HP is less than half (24) and purple when the HP is less than one-fourth (12). Once the color is changed, it does not change back even if the HP is recovered."},{"title":"► Juice Splash/7 (14)/Fortitude/Negates","description":"Sprays juice around itself. Within \"Range: Caster\" deals 2d+2 magic damage to \"1 area (3m radius)/5\".\nIf the color of the monster is red, the target is blinded for 1 day after failing the resistance check. If the color of the monster is purple, the Gradient Plum gains a +2 bonus to the Standard Values of this unique skill. Damage and its accompanying effects are all of the disease types.\nThis unique skill costs 5 MP.\n2d |\nLoot |\n2 -8 |\nNothing |\n9 - 12 |\nDiffused Fruit Juice (150G/Green A) |\n13+ |\nConcentrated Fruit Juice (650G/Green A) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Gradient Plum","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"VcCTfW4ZGa2GNsCp","name":"Daemonoid Ivy","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:daemonoid-ivy","level":9,"monsterType":"Plant","intelligence":"None","perception":"Magic","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Wilderness","reputation":17,"weakness":19,"weakPoint":"Fire damage +3 points","initiative":15,"movementSpeed":"10 (Dependent)","fortitude":"13 (20)","willpower":"12 (19)","source":"Natural History of Ursyla p. 128","description":"A variant of Marionette Ivy that has been frequently sighted in the border regions of Zamsaska territory.\n\nWhile it parasitically entwines itself around corpses and moves in a similar way, the intertwined vines distinctively grow into shapes reminiscent of Daemons , which is theorized to be due to the influence of the Abyss.\n\nThough it wanders in search of its next host, just like the original species, it has become more aggressive and dangerous. These vines are in high demand among researchers as they provide clues for studying the Abyss and Daemons, but rumors suggest that some unscrupulous individuals have been illegally distributing them as materials for dangerous \"Evil Vines\" (see Natural History of Ursyla , p. 40).","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Psychic Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯ 2 Actions","description":"It can perform 2 Major Actions in 1 round."},{"title":"⏩False Form Release","description":"This effect can only be used when the creature's current HP is at or below half of its maximum HP (rounded up). It completely unravels its Daemon form that it had woven, allowing all vines to move freely.\nThereafter, this monster gains \"3 Actions\" (can perform 3 Major Actions in 1 round), and additionally, whenever its vine attacks or [►Snaring Vines] succeed, it deals 1 extra point of Curse fixed damage to the target.\nThis effect automatically ends when this monster's current HP exceeds half of its maximum HP, and it returns to its Daemon-like form."},{"title":"►Snaring Vines / 13 (20) / Fortitude / Negates","description":"Wraps vines around \"Target: 1 Character\" at \"Range: Touch.\" The target becomes unable to move and receives a -4 penalty modifier to Evasion checks. These effects do not stack even if received multiple times.\nWhen the target attempts to escape, follow the de-bonding rules .\nThis monster has numerous vines and can maintain existing [►Snaring Vines] on characters while attempting melee attacks or new [►Snaring Vines], regardless of how many targets are already ensnared."},{"title":"◯ Delicate Loot","description":"The quantity of loot Abyssal Vines is reduced by the number of times this monster received Fire-type damage during combat (minimum 0).\n2d |\nLoot |\nAlways |\nAbyssal Vines (250G/Gold Green A) x 1d |\n2 - 7 |\nNothing |\n8 - 10 |\nRemains of the Dead (500G/White A) |\n11+ |\nExpensive Heirlooms (1,000G/Gold White S) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Daemonoid Ivy","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"YguuCWllU9K5yUCA","name":"Dracaena Tree","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:dracaena-tree","level":5,"monsterType":"Plant","intelligence":"Average","perception":"Magic","disposition":"Neutral","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Forests, Caves","reputation":13,"weakness":16,"weakPoint":"Fire damage +3 points","initiative":12,"movementSpeed":"10","fortitude":"8 (15)","willpower":"7 (14)","source":"Ancient Blue (SW2.5 supplement) p. 136","description":"This is a tree that mimics the form of a dragon. While it spreads its branches and leaves widely to create wings, it cannot actually fly. It can attack by spitting exploding seeds that scatter fragments in the surrounding area from the part that mimics a mouth. However, due to its gentle and timid nature, it will not initiate an attack unless it is attacked first.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯Dragon Mimicry / 6 (13) / Detect Check","description":"Mimics the form of a dragon. Even if a Monster Knowledge check is performed against this monster, it will be identified as a Draconet .\nIf a Detect check against Target Number 13 is performed on this monster and succeeds, you recognize that it is not a Draconet and can perform a normal Monster Knowledge check.\nBody"},{"title":"►Seed Burst / 6 (13) / Fortitude / Half","description":"From the part mimicking a dragon's mouth, it forcefully launches seeds that explode. Using \"Range/Area: 1 (10m) / Shot ,\" deals 2d+3 points of Bludgeoning magic damage to targets in \"1 area (3m radius) / 5\".\nThis ability cannot be used in consecutive turns.\nWing"},{"title":"🗨Power Strike I","description":"Increases damage by +4 points. As a risk, the declared section receives a -2 penalty to Evasion checks.\n2d |\nLoot |\n2 - 7 |\nNothing |\n8 - 10 |\nExploded Seed Fragments (150G/Green A) x 1d |\n11+ |\nExploded Seed Fragments (150G/Green A) x 2d |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Dracaena Tree","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"ZFBohJ5slbYyBMDC","name":"Daemonwood Branch","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:daemonwood-branch","level":13,"monsterType":"Plant","intelligence":"Low","perception":"Magic","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Forests","reputation":18,"weakness":21,"weakPoint":"Fire damage + 3 points","initiative":19,"movementSpeed":"20","fortitude":"17 (24)","willpower":"14 (21)","source":"Monstrous Lore p. 130","description":"The Daemonwood tree can shed its branches that have become too thick, which in turn can transform into a humanoid creature. These creatures, known as Daemonwood Branches, are naked and wander the forest hunting animals (and occasionally Humanoids, Barbarous, or Mythical Beasts).\n\nThey bring their catch to their master, the Daemonwood, burying them in the ground for nourishment.\n\nDespite their low intellect, Daemonwood Branches have good instincts to detect danger. If they feel that the person they have found is too strong for them, they will attempt to lure them to their master, leaving obvious tracks behind.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"► Daemon Transformation","description":"The monster transforms into any type of Daemon of 12 th level or lower, and all HP and MP are restored, and all effects it had been receiving are also lost. From its next turn, it acts as the Daemon completely.\nIf it dies, it returns to its original form. In that case, when looting this monster, use this monster table instead of Daemon's with added +2 bonus to the loot rolls.\n2d |\nLoot |\n2 - 9 |\nGray Bark (400G/Green A) |\n10+ |\nMagic Bark (4,000G/Gold Green S) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Daemonwood Branch","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"azaTGRUidH0Iyjpn","name":"Spinel Hood","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:spinel-hood","level":7,"monsterType":"Plant","intelligence":"Animal","perception":"Five senses (Darkvision)","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Forests, Shallows","reputation":13,"weakness":17,"weakPoint":"Bludgeoning damage +3 points","initiative":14,"movementSpeed":"/","fortitude":"9 (16)","willpower":"9 (16)","source":"AB, p. 95","description":"This is a dark purple, translucent slime mold that attaches to and parasitizes the neck and back of Animal, Humanoids, and Barbarous creatures. It got its name because the translucent substance covering the host's neck and back resembles a hood made of gems. The Spinel Hood survives by stealing some of its host's food.\n\nIn a Shallow, the Spinel Hood splits once every few months and seeks out new hosts. Outside of a Shallow, it does not split.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯Psychic Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯Host-Dependent","description":"All sections of this monster except its Main Section, as well as various numerical values, depend on the host it has parasitized. Please substitute the host's values for any placeholder values in the various statistics and data. If the host has multiple sections, the Main Section automatically changes to Hood section. The evasion of Hood section is calculated based on the evasion of sections containing the head or neck. If there are multiple qualifying sections, the GM determines which to use. The GM also determines whether it becomes a target of [◯Attack Obstacle] and similar effects.\nSpecial effects and abilities generally use the same data as original, but anything dependent on language, including magic, cannot be used.\nHood"},{"title":"◯Parasitic Hood","description":"This monster parasitizes characters that are level (Adventurer or Monster Level) 6 or below and either Humanoid , Barbarous , or Animal .\nOnce parasitism occurs, regardless of the host, it gains \"Perception: Five Senses (Darkvision)\", \"Intellect: Animal\", and \"Language: None.\"\nIf the Hood section's HP can be reduced to 0 before destroying the host (or Main Section in case of multiple sections), the host is freed. However, they cannot perform actions (movement, Major Action, Minor Actions) for 1 week afterward. Furthermore, they receive a -2 penalty to all skill checks for the following month.\n2d |\nLoot |\nAlways |\nAbyss Shard (200G/-) |\n2 - 12 |\nTranslucent Fragments (50G/Gold Black B) |\n13+ |\nLarge Translucent Fragments (500G/Gold Black A) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Spinel Hood","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"g7rcV32T7NLBuPtr","name":"Beartrap Creeper","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:beartrap-creeper","level":6,"monsterType":"Plant","intelligence":"None","perception":"Magic","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Forests, Grasslands","reputation":13,"weakness":15,"weakPoint":"Fire Damage +3","initiative":12,"movementSpeed":"9 (Crawling)","fortitude":"11 (18)","willpower":"9 (16)","source":"Natural History of Ursyla p. 127","description":"This is a climbing plant that captures animals native to the Great Sebrae Forest. It has leaves about 80-100cm in diameter that resemble bear traps used for hunting. The leaves secrete acids that digest animals and use their gripping force to catch prey and extract nutrients. Despite its trap-like name, rather than waiting in one place, it actively moves around to hunt its prey.\n\nYoung Bear Trap Creepers only have one trap-like leaf, but as they grow, they have been observed to develop up to five leaves. The acid produced by Bear Trap Creepers is sometimes used in seasoning and the production of fermented foods.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Psychic Immunity","description":"Stolon"},{"title":"◯ Recovery = 6 points","description":"At the end of the turn, all the Stolon section and Leaf sections recover 6 HP each. This ability has no effect on sections that have already reached 0 HP. If the HP of the Stolon section falls to 0 or below, this ability is lost.\nLeaf"},{"title":"◯ Bear Trap","description":"When the trap leaf's attack hits, it clamps down on the target. The target becomes immobilized and receives a -2 penalty modifier to Evasion checks. Additionally, from the next turn, the clamping Leaf section can secrete acid as a Major Action, dealing 2d points of Poison magic damage to the target with \"Resistance: Can't.\" Even if multiple Leaf sections clamp onto the same character, the penalty modifier to Evasion checks does not stack.\nWhen the target attempts to escape, follow the de-bonding rules . While clamping a target with this ability, the Leaf section cannot perform any melee attacks. If this monster wishes to release the target itself, it can do so automatically as a Minor Action.\n2d |\nLoot |\nAlways |\nEnergetic Roots (100G / Green A) |\n2 - 8 |\nNothing |\n9+ |\nAcid Sap (450G / Green A) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Beartrap Creeper","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"gdcPuCRiUCXKKfmb","name":"Poison Pollen","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:poison-pollen","level":3,"monsterType":"Plant","intelligence":"None","perception":"Magic","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Forests, Lakesides, Caves","reputation":10,"weakness":13,"weakPoint":"Fire damage +3","initiative":8,"movementSpeed":"-/10(Floating)","fortitude":"6 (13)","willpower":"4 (11)","source":"BM","description":"A monster made of toxic pollen that has solidified into a floating ball with a diameter of approximately 50cm. They are said to have almost no will of their own, and respond to attacks by external threats by scattering poison and poisoning them.\n\nThey can be found floating in windy places, and also within caves populated by other plants.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Poison, Disease, and Psychic Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯ Powder Body","description":"The Poison Pollen is immune to critical hits from all weapon attacks."},{"title":"► Pollen Attack / Can't","description":"The Pollen sticks itself to the target's mucous membranes, causing damage. This has \"Range: Touch\" and deals 1d+1 poison magic damage to \"Target: 1 Character.\""},{"title":"◯ Pollen Poison / 5 (12) / Fortitude / Negates","description":"Characters who suffer 1 or more points of damage from [ ► Pollen Attack] receive a -1 penalty to their Action Checks for 3 minutes (18 rounds). This effect can stack up to two times (for a total penalty of -2) and is of the Poison type.\n2d |\nLoot |\n2 - 7 |\nNothing |\n8+ |\nPollen Ball (60G / Green B) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Poison Pollen","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"hN5tmnayhEKP9uMm","name":"Entlet","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:entlet","level":7,"monsterType":"Plant","intelligence":"Average","perception":"Magic","disposition":"Neutral","soulscars":0,"languages":"Sylvan","habitat":"Forest","reputation":12,"weakness":18,"weakPoint":"Fire damage +3 points","initiative":10,"movementSpeed":"12","fortitude":"10 (17)","willpower":"10 (17)","source":"CR II p. 366","description":"A giant tree that roams around, using its roots as feet to walk. Entlets are said to be over 100 years old and have a wide variety of knowledge they can be persuaded to share with others. Their leaves are reportedly herbs that increase one's wisdom, and teas brewed with them are top-rated among mothers. Entlets tend to be gentle giants and will be friendly if treated in kind.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"► Fairy Magic 6 Level/Magic Power 8 (15)","description":"It can use Earth, Water/Ice, Light, and Dark types."},{"title":"◯ 🗨 ► Magic Aptitude","description":"They can use the Combat Feats [ Targeting ], [ Hawk Eye ], [ Metamagic/Targets ], and [ Wordbreak ].\n2d |\nLoot |\nAlways |\nEnt Leaves (100G/Green A) |\n2 - 6 |\nNothing |\n7 - 12 |\nMysterious Seeds (100G/Green A) |\n13+ |\nMysterious Sapling (500G/Green A) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Entlet","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"iEhIOLVtqEWe41Bw","name":"Night Wanderer","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:night-wanderer","level":8,"monsterType":"Plant","intelligence":"None","perception":"Magic","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Forests","reputation":15,"weakness":18,"weakPoint":"Physical damage +2","initiative":14,"movementSpeed":"10 (Many Legs)","fortitude":"11 (18)","willpower":"10 (17)","source":"Natural History of Dorden p. 126","description":"This is a plant monster with a large fruit resembling the upper body of a Humanoid female, from which writhing thorny vines grow.\n\nDuring the day, it lies on the ground, concealing its fruit part with thorns, and becomes active at night. It primarily captures and kills animals living in grasslands, dissolving them with corrosive liquid injected from its thorny spines to obtain nutrients, but Humanoids and Barbarous may also fall victim. Its nocturnal wandering appearance has sometimes led to it being mistaken for Undead.\n\nIt automatically counterattacks aggressors with its thorns. It also launches attacks that are difficult to evade, enveloping targets with its thorny vines.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯Poison, Disease, Psychic Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯Soft Body","description":"All sections are treated as having 3 more Defense points against blunt weapons."},{"title":"◯Delicate Loot","description":"If the HP of the Fruit section drops to 0 or less due to magic damage, the loot of \"Rich Fruit\" will be lost.\nFruit"},{"title":"◯Vivid Spray /10 (17) / Fortitude / Half","description":"When receiving 1 or more points of applied damage from a bladed weapon, it scatters a juice spray. The attacker immediately takes 1d+2 points of magic damage and becomes blinded.\nThe blinding effect lasts for 3 minutes (18 rounds) until an effect that removes blindness is received or until a Major Action is taken to \"wipe the eyes\". The magic damage and blinding effect are treated as Poison type."},{"title":"◯Magic Power Restoration = 5 points","description":"If its MP is below 10 at the start of its turn, it will recover 5 MP."},{"title":"►Phantasma / 10 (17) / Willpower / Negates","description":"By appearing as a fragile being or in a form that evokes a protective instinct, it makes others hesitate to attack. One target character within \"Range: 1 (10m)\" becomes unable to perform any action that causes physical damage or magical damage to either Fruit or Thorn sections for 10 seconds (1 round).\nThis effect is treated as a Psychic type.\nUsing this effect consumes 5 MP points from the Fruit section."},{"title":"►Counter Stance","description":"Spreads all Thorn sections along the ground and make them take a counter-attack stance. All Thorn sections gain a +1 bonus to Accuracy checks for 10 seconds (1 round) and are treated as if they have learned the Combat Feat [ Counter ]. Simultaneously, they receive a -1 penalty to Evasion during the effect duration.\nUsing this effect consumes 5 MP points for each Thorn section that gains the effect.\nThorn"},{"title":"►Enveloping Attack / 12(19) / Evasion check / Negates","description":"Attacks by enveloping with all thorns, dealing 2d+7 points of physical damage. This ability can only be used if all Thorn sections with 1 or more HP have not acted yet, and when used, all Thorn sections will complete their Major Action.\nIf 2 Thorn sections use this ability, the physical damage dealt is increased by +5 points, and if it's 3 sections, it's increased by +10 points.\nAdditionally, this ability triggers [○Decaying Poison]. Furthermore, if its 2 Thorns sections, it gains a +1 bonus to the Success Value of the Decaying Poison, and the damage dealt is increased by +2 points. If it's 3 sections, it gains a +2 bonus to the Success Value, and the damage dealt is increased by +4 points."},{"title":"►Thorn Protection","description":"Envelops itself and its Fruit section with thorns, defending and injuring attackers. For 10 seconds (1 round), if someone attempts to use a melee attack or \"Range: Touch\" effect against the Thorn section and Fruit section, after resolving that effect, those targets receive fixed damage equal to \"the current round number\" points.\nThis ability can only be used by one Thorn section per round. Additionally, the Thorn section using this ability does not gain the effect of the Fruit section's [►Counter Stance].\nIf a Melee Attack is performed on the Fruit section during this ability's effect duration, and the conditions for both [◯Vivid Spray] and this ability's effect are met, this ability takes priority in resolution."},{"title":"◯Decaying Poison / 11(18) / Fortitude / Negates","description":"The target hit by a melee attack and the unique skill [►Enveloping Attack] receives 3 points of magic damage and suffers a -1 penalty to Accuracy and Evasion checks for 3 minutes (18 rounds). The penalty accumulates up to -3.\nBoth the damage and penalty are treated as poison-type effects."},{"title":"◯Attack Obstacle = +4・+4","description":"The thorns obstruct attacks.\nThe Fruit section gains a +4 bonus to Evasion checks against Melee Attack and Ranged Attack.\nThis effect is lost when any of the Thorn sections' HP drops to 0 or below.\n2d |\nLoot |\nAlways |\nRich Fruit (1,000G/Green A) x 1d |\n2 - 9 |\nNothing |\n10-12 |\nMagical Vine (600G/Green A) |\n10-12 |\nBewitching Vine (1,200G/Green A) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Night Wanderer","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"k0443XNqVzPVEZ7y","name":"Hundred Bouquet","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:hundred-bouquet","level":3,"monsterType":"Plant","intelligence":"None","perception":"Magic","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Forests, Marshes, Waterfront","reputation":11,"weakness":13,"weakPoint":"Slashing damage +3 points","initiative":9,"movementSpeed":"8 (Floating)","fortitude":"5 (12)","willpower":"4 (11)","source":"Natural History of Ursyla , p. 127","description":"These are floating clusters of countless deep navy blue flowers found in the Great Sebrae Forest, forming hemispheres about 1-1.5m in diameter. The name comes from their resemblance to large bouquets. With no leaves and deep navy blue stems, when growing on the ground, they appear as if large bouquets have been placed there.\n\nAt the base of the stem, there are white hyphae that look like bundled strings, and these hyphae live symbiotically with the flower seeds throughout the forest. Several times a year, when expanding their habitat, the hyphae decompose to produce gas, causing the flowers to bloom and float. While the decomposition gas and pollen have a very sweet, pleasant fragrance, they are toxic.\n\nThe hyphae absorb the nutrients from animals that die from this poison, growing into the next generation of Hundred Bouquets.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯Poison, Disease, and Psychic Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯Adhesion","description":"When a Slam attack hits, it adheres to the target with fungal filaments. From the next turn, at the start of this monster's turn, it automatically deals 1d points of poison magic damage to the target with \"Resistance: Can't.\" When the target makes weapon attacks against this monster, physical damage is reduced by 4 points.\nWhen the target attempts to escape, follow the de-bonding rules . While adhering to the target by this ability, this monster cannot move on its own, and its position (area, coordinate) is always shared with the target. Additionally, it cannot perform any Slam attacks. If this monster wishes to release the target, it can do so automatically as a Minor Action."},{"title":"►Poison Powder Gas Burst / 4 (11) / Fortitude / Half","description":"Spreads pollen-mixed poison gas in \"Range: Caster\" targeting \"1 Area (3m radius) / 5.\" Each target takes 2d points of Poison magic damage.\nThis effect cannot be used in consecutive turns."},{"title":"◯Delicate Loot","description":""}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"2 - 5","loot":"|"},{"roll":"6 - 9","loot":"|"},{"roll":"10 - 13","loot":"|"},{"roll":"14+","loot":"|"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Hundred Bouquet","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"k67oz2WIIuv4FZUp","name":"Megalomor","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:megalomor","level":15,"monsterType":"Plant","intelligence":"High","perception":"Magic","disposition":"Neutral","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Forests, Meadows","reputation":20,"weakness":24,"weakPoint":"Physical damage +2 points","initiative":20,"movementSpeed":"-","fortitude":"20 (27)","willpower":"18 (25)","source":"Monstrous Lore p. 130","description":"Megalomor is a massive perennial herb that can grow several meters high with stems and leaves. It thrives in areas with heavy pollution, such as poison or dense mana, and is known to eliminate them.\n\nIt is not considered a threat unless touched, but the juice of its leaves has potent disease-curing properties. People with power and wealth sometimes hire others to collect the leaves. Megalomor sometimes grows in areas where Mako Stones can be mined in abundance because of its mana- removing properties. It is sometimes requested to be exterminated, but some Barbarous who prefer a polluted environment may try to kill it. In such cases, the plant will defend itself with all its might.\n\nIf left alone, Megalomor will eventually die out without leaving anything behind when pollution and mana levels in the environment are sufficiently reduced. How this non-flowering, non-fruit-bearing, and non-bulb- producing plant continues to grow and reappear in new places remains a mystery.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Poison Immunity, ◯ Disease Immunity, ◯ Curse Immunity, ◯ Psychic Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯ Mana Interference","description":"If this monster succeeds in any Willpower check, treat resistance as \"Negates\".\nStem"},{"title":"◯ 2 Actions","description":"Can perform two Major Actions in one round."},{"title":"► Devour Mana/19 (26)/Willpower/Negates","description":"Megalomor absorbs mana from surrounding entities and regains life force.\n\"Target: All Areas (30m Radius) / All\" are dealt magic damage to MP of (1/10 of the target's current MP (rounded up)) within \"Range: Caster\".\nAfter that, the HP of the Stem section is recovered by the sum of the applied damage."},{"title":"► Full Wave Release/20 (27)","description":"Megalomor releases a wave that removes all effects on \"Range: Caster\" and \"Target: All areas (30m radius) / All\".\nThis unique skill Success Value is compared with the Success values of all effects to be removed, and if Success Value is higher, those effects are canceled.\nHowever, the effects of poison and disease types are automatically canceled. Using this effect consumes 15 MP.\nLeaf"},{"title":"🗨 △ Cover I","description":"The effect is the same as the combat feat [ Cover I ]. Exceptionally, a Leaf can only cover a Stem section."},{"title":"◯ Bloodsucking","description":"If the Leaf hits, the HP of the Leaf section is restored by the same value as the applied damage.\n2d |\nLoot |\n2 - 7 |\nMedicinal Leaf Liquid (500G/Gold Green A) |\n8 - 10 |\nMedicine Leaf Liquid (2,500G/Green S) |\n11+ |\nSacred Medicine Leaf Liquid (5,000G/Green S) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Megalomor","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"kTQsrSjUnrvZL2AB","name":"Rockwool Fluff","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:rockwool-fluff","level":1,"monsterType":"Plant","intelligence":"None","perception":"Magic","disposition":"Neutral","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Plains, Forests, Shallows","reputation":8,"weakness":12,"weakPoint":"Bludgeoning damage +3 points","initiative":8,"movementSpeed":"-/5 (Floating)","fortitude":"2 (9)","willpower":"1 (8)","source":"AB, p. 94","description":"These seeds of the Rock Lotus Tree float gently through the air until they reach their destination. While they appear as pink, sparkling cotton-like tufts about 30cm in diameter, they are actually composed of extremely fine needle-like fibers. When exposed to strong impacts, they burst and scatter their seeds in the surrounding area.\n\nIt is said they have a tendency to drift and gather in places where Abyss Shards are present.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯Psychic Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯Fluff Burst","description":"When HP drops to 0 or below, it explodes.\nWithin \"Range: Caster,\" it deals 1 point of fixed damage to \"Target: 1 Area (3m radius) / 5\", after which it is automatically removed from the game.\nInside a Shallow Abyss, the damage increases to \"2\" points.\nOther Rockwool Fluffs and Rock Lotus Trees receive no damage from this effect.\n2d |\nLoot |\n2 - 11 |\nNothing |\n12+ |\nAbyss Shard (200G/-) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Rockwool Fluff","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"kxGb477WX0EV8fTu","name":"Giant Balloon Seed","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:giant-balloon-seed","level":3,"monsterType":"Plant","intelligence":"None","perception":"Magic","disposition":"Neutral","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Forests, Swamps","reputation":10,"weakness":13,"weakPoint":"Fire Damage +3","initiative":10,"movementSpeed":"8 (4 Legs)/-","fortitude":"4 (11)","willpower":"3 (10)","source":"Battle Mastery p. 123","description":"Giant Balloon Seeds were first cultivated during the Magitech Civilization but have since begun to grow wild. They resemble flowering plants of about 3 meters in length and attack by firing fist-sized seeds from their flower. They are capable of using their roots as legs to move about and these extended vines to protect their flowers from attack. Some individual Giant Balloon Seeds have grown in size and possess a greater number of flowers.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Psychic Immunity","description":"Vine"},{"title":"◯ Substitution","description":"When the Flower section suffers damage from a melee or ranged attack, either Vine section can take the damage instead. The damage applied to the Flower applied as-is to the Vine (without recalculation). This unique skill can only be used once per round for each Vine.\nGiant Balloon Seed cannot use this unique skill against ranged or melee with multiple targets or wide-area attacks.\n2d |\nLoot |\nAlways |\nHard Seed (30G / Green B) |\n2 - 9 |\nNothing |\n10+ |\nBeautiful Bulb (300G / Green A) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Giant Balloon Seed","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"mFK67YVD9AYlQO2u","name":"Gravity Root","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:gravity-root","level":13,"monsterType":"Plant","intelligence":"None","perception":"Magic","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Forests, Swamps","reputation":17,"weakness":20,"weakPoint":"Wind Damage +3","initiative":17,"movementSpeed":"-/20 (Floating)","fortitude":"15(22)","willpower":"15(22)","source":"BM","description":"This is a plant that floats by its roots and absorbs nutrients from the atmosphere. The total height of the plant is about 3 meters, but the root part is heavier than a piece of iron of the same size. How it floats is a mystery, and the wise men who are trying to figure it out are eagerly waiting for the roots to be brought back.\n\nGravity Roots can control gravity around itself, preventing flight and movement, and send leaves flying like arrows to finish off prey.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Psychic Immunity","description":"Root"},{"title":"◯ Gravity Wedge / 16 (23) / Willpower / Negates","description":"It alters gravity, increasing weight and burden and interfering with the actions of creatures. Within \"Ranger: Caster\" and \"Target: All Areas (30m Radius)/Space,\" must perform a Willpower check at the start of each turn, and if they fail, their movement is halved (rounded up) for 10 seconds (1 round) and they cannot fly.\nFurthermore, if the success value of the resistance for this unique skill is 4 or more points lower than the Target Number, the character will fall prone and will not be able to perform any movement, Minor Actions or declare Combat Feats for the same duration.\nLeaf"},{"title":"◯ Swarm","description":"When targeting the Gravity Root or another character in the same skirmish with a ranged attack or magic, the Combat Feats [ Targeting ] and [ Magic Control ] cannot be used.\nIf all Leaf sections fall to 0 HP or lower, this unique skill cannot be used."},{"title":"► Throw Leaves","description":"The Bladed Leaf attack can be performed as a thrown attack with \"Range: 1 Area (30m).\" Accuracy check and damage are the same as for normal attacks, and the number of leaves is infinite.\n2d |\nLoot |\nAlways |\nHeavy Root (2,300G / Gold Green Black S) |\n2 - 8 |\nNothing |\n9 - 12 |\nKeenly Sharpened Leaves (500G / Green A) |\n13+ |\nKeenly Sharpened Leaves (500G / Green A) x 1d |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Gravity Root","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"mkuNiDGISi5SkfWZ","name":"Balloon Lotus","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:balloon-lotus","level":5,"monsterType":"Plant","intelligence":"None","perception":"Magic","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Plains, Wilderness, Shallows","reputation":11,"weakness":14,"weakPoint":"Bludgeoning damage +3 points","initiative":11,"movementSpeed":"5 (Crawling) / 10 (Floating)","fortitude":"9 (16)","willpower":"7 (14)","source":"AB, p. 95","description":"This is a floating, drifting lotus flower with an inverted top and bottom. At the top, there is a large, balloon-like pure white root, and from this root grow leaves that are large, hard, and have serrated edges, along with translucent light purple glass-like lotus petals.\n\nThe white root has the ability to keep this floating lotus airborne, typically hovering between 2-5 meters in the air. If the root is cut off, it loses its floating ability. Along with flowers, it also bears fruit, which can be forcefully ejected, allowing it to take root in the bodies of animals and plants.\n\nThe root has a spongy texture with numerous holes and is used as a food ingredient.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯Psychic Immunity","description":"Root"},{"title":"◯Attack Obstacle +4 • None","description":"By floating the entire structure in midair it hinders attacks.\nAll sections of this monster gain a +4 bonus to Evasion checks against melee attacks.\nIf the Root section's HP falls to 0 or below, this effect is lost."},{"title":"◯Securing Field of Fire","description":"By levitating the entire structure in midair, it grants Flower and Leaves sections a field of fire and ranged attack capabilities.\nFlower and Leaves sections are considered to have learned the Combat Feats [ Targeting ] and [ Hawk Eye ], and each can use the [… Projectile] ability.\nWhen the Root section's HP falls to 0 or below, those sections lose their [… Projectile] ability.\nFlower ◯Seed Projectile\nIf the Root section has 1 or more HP, it can perform a thrown attack using seeds with \"Range: 2(30m).\" Accuracy check and damage use normal data."},{"title":"►Root Regeneration (Shallow)","description":"This effect can only be used within Shallow Abysses. Restores Root section's HP up to Flower section's current HP. Regeneration is possible even if Root section's HP is already 0 or below, and Root section can utilize all of its abilities.\nWhen using this effect, the Flower section's HP becomes 0.\nLeaf"},{"title":"◯Leaf Blade Projectile","description":"If the Root section has 1 or more HP, it can perform a thrown attack using serrated leaves with \"Range: 2 (30m).\" Accuracy check and damage use normal data.\n2d |\nLoot |\nAlways |\nFloating Root (220G/Gold Green A) |\n2 - 10 |\nNothing |\n11+ |\nAbyss Shard (200G/-) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Balloon Lotus","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"p1AxStUqbo0z7tUU","name":"Tentacle Kelp","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:tentacle-kelp","level":7,"monsterType":"Plant","intelligence":"Animal","perception":"Magic","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Oceans, Shores","reputation":14,"weakness":17,"weakPoint":"Slashing type damage +3 points","initiative":15,"movementSpeed":"10 (Many Legs) / 10 (Swimming)","fortitude":"11(18)","willpower":"10(17)","source":"BM","description":"Tentacle Kelp is a mobile form of seagrass, about 5 meters long. It entangles and preys on animals and boats mainly in shallow water, but it can also walk by its roots and may come up to beaches and other areas when there is no prey.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Water/Ice Immunity, ◯ Psychic Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯ Underwater Aptitude","description":"Leaf"},{"title":"◯ Entangling Leaves","description":"A successful hit from a Wrap entangles the target. Each round, the entangled target is unable to move, is hit automatically by the Wrap and makes all Accuracy and Evasion Checks with a -2 penalty. This penalty is not cumulative.\nWhen the target tries to escape, use de-bonding rules.\nWhile entangled by this unique skill, the Leaf section cannot attack other characters. If the monster itself wants to release the target, it can do so with a Minor Action.\nRoot"},{"title":"◯ Attitude Control","description":"Tentacle Kelp cannot fall prone.\nIf the Root section falls to 0 HP or lower, this unique skill cannot be used."},{"title":"◯ Standing Firm","description":"If the Leaves section attempts to use de-bonding, its success value is given a +2 bonus.\nIf the Root section falls to 0 HP or lower, this unique skill cannot be used.\n2d |\nLoot |\n2 - 8 |\nNothing |\n9+ |\nFresh Seaweed (240G / Green A) x 1d |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Tentacle Kelp","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"pbyL8VH6xH03VxZ7","name":"Dancing Thorn","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:dancing-thorn","level":3,"monsterType":"Plant","intelligence":"None","perception":"Magic","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Meadow, Wilderness","reputation":10,"weakness":12,"weakPoint":"Fire damage +3 points","initiative":11,"movementSpeed":"10 (Rotation)","fortitude":"5 (12)","willpower":"4 (11)","source":"CR I p. 414","description":"These thorns are as tall as a Humanoid. They are constant rustling and shaking, even when there is no wind. When an animal approaches, the thorns detach their roots, curl up and spin around, and strike the animal, attempting to tear it apart with the numerous thorns on their stems. If the thorns are defeated or driven away, they may reestablish their roots and grow again with renewed vigor, so it is hard to get rid of this weed.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Painful Strike","description":"If the 2d roll of the damage roll is 10 or more, the damage is increased by an additional +3 points.\n2d |\nLoot |\n2 - 8 |\nNothing |\n9+ |\nCrimson Petals (120G/Green A) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Dancing Thorn","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"ppYgS5LguklPPNSg","name":"Big Archer","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:big-archer","level":6,"monsterType":"Plant","intelligence":"None","perception":"Magic","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Forests","reputation":10,"weakness":15,"weakPoint":"Fire damage +3","initiative":7,"movementSpeed":"-/-","fortitude":"8 (15)","willpower":"6 (13)","source":"Battle Mastery p. 124","description":"This plant hides on the ground, similar to Needle Archers . However, the needles launched by Big Archers are much more resilient and can carry a couple of different debilitating poisons as well.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Psychic Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯ Vine Network","description":"A Big Archer has thin vines stretching out 2-3 Areas (10m Radius) around itself. If characters don't successfully make a Danger Sense check against Target Number of 16, they will step into it unknowingly and become surprised by Big Archer.\nIn the event of a Surprise attack, the Big Archer is placed in the Frontline Area in Simplified Combat. In Standard and Advanced Combat, all PCs are placed within a 10m radius of the monster."},{"title":"◯ Flying Needles","description":"A Needle attack can also be performed as a shooting attack with \"Range: 1 (10m).\""},{"title":"◯ No Blind Spot","description":"Within the [ ◯ Vine Network], a Big Archer can ignore shielding (Standard/Advanced Combat) with Needle attacks, and will not suffer Stray Shots if it shoots into the skirmish."},{"title":"◯ Poison Needles / 8 (15) / Fortitude / Negates","description":"The Big Archer has two possible poisons it can use with its Needles. If the Big Archer deals 1 or more applied damage with their Needle attack, the target must immediately make a Fortitude check.\nRotting Poison: If the target fails to resist, they receive an extra 7 Poison-type damage.\nParalyzing Poison: If the target fails to resist, they receive a -2 penalty to Accuracy and Evasion checks for 10 seconds (1 round). This effect is not cumulative."},{"title":"🗨 Million Needles","description":"A Big Archer may attack all characters (enemies and allies) within range of the [ ◯ Vine Network] simultaneously during its turn.\n2d |\nLoot |\n2 - 4 |\nNothing |\n5 - 8 |\nPoisonous Needle (50G / Green B) |\n9+ |\nStrong Vine (300G / Green A) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Big Archer","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"qURnyGh6Svngt7f8","name":"Mandrake","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:mandrake","level":5,"monsterType":"Plant","intelligence":"Low","perception":"Magic","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Forests","reputation":11,"weakness":16,"weakPoint":"Physical Damage +2","initiative":8,"movementSpeed":"7","fortitude":"7 (14)","willpower":"8 (15)","source":"Battle Mastery p. 124","description":"A plant whose roots are shaped like a human. The root is about 60cm in length and is typically buried in soil most of the year, with only the head, from which a small amount of leaves grow, exposed. Under normal circumstances, a Mandrake will prefer to grow in dimly-lit sections of deep forests, and have distinctive pale, pink flowers.\n\nAs winter grows near, the Mandrake will uproot itself and wander in search of a mate, looking to create a new batch of seeds.\n\nDue to their purported uses in medicines and other concoctions, Mandrakes have been overhunted by both Humanoids and Barbarous, and so hold grudges against both groups. A Mandrake can call upon Fairy magic in order to help protect itself, as well as the signature screaming, they are known for. It's said that those who hear the scream and live will still be afflicted with any number of mental disorders.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"► Fairy Magic 4 Level / Magic Power 6 (13)","description":"The types used are Earth, Water/Ice, Light and Dark. This does not change even if the contract pattern is adopted (see MA, p. 136)."},{"title":"◯ Scream / 10 &amp; 14 / Fortitude &amp; Willpower / Negates","description":"Once per day, when it suffers HP damage, the Mandrake can unleash a terrifying, deadly scream.\nCharacter in \"Range: Caster\" and \"Target: All Areas (30m Radius)/All\" around Mandrake must immediately make both a Fortitude and Willpower check. The target must immediately perform a Fortitude check with a Target Number of 10. If the target fails to do so, it is immediately unconscious and remains unconscious for 1 hour unless it is restored by a spell such as [ Awaken ].\nIf the Fortitude succeeds, the next must be Willpower with a Target Number of 14. Characters that fail the subsequent Willpower check cannot perform any Major or Minor Actions and receive a -4 penalty to Evasion for 10 seconds (1 round).\n2d |\nLoot |\nAlways |\nVitality Root (100G / Green A) |\n2 - 11 |\nNothing |\n12+ |\nMandrake Seed (1500G / Green S) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Mandrake","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"sHhLtJzIA9B5ipW2","name":"Living Tree","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:living-tree","level":10,"monsterType":"Plant","intelligence":"Low","perception":"Magic","disposition":"Neutral","soulscars":0,"languages":"Sylvan","habitat":"Forest","reputation":15,"weakness":21,"weakPoint":"Fire damage + 3 points","initiative":16,"movementSpeed":"14","fortitude":"15 (22)","willpower":"13 (20)","source":"CR III p. 357","description":"These are giant walking trees that boast of their huge size and monstrous strength. Some trees are around 5 meters tall and more than 1,000 years old.\n\nThey are not very intelligent, but they are mild-mannered and honest. They are proud to be the protectors of the forest and can become friends with anyone they meet as long as they are respectful and considerate of the forest.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"► Fairy Magic 2 Level/Magic Power 3 (10)","description":"Can use Earth, Water/Ice, Light, and Dark types."},{"title":"🗨 Power Strike II","description":"They can deal an additional +12 damage on their next attack. However, any Evasion Check made by them this turn receives a -2 penalty."},{"title":"🗨 Improved Aimed Attack","description":"When attacking, the Living Tree can gain a +4 bonus to Accuracy but receives a -8 penalty to damage dealt when doing so."},{"title":"◯ Regeneration = 10 points","description":"At the end of each round, Living Tree recovers 10 HP. This has no effect if the Living Tree has 0 HP or lower.\n2d |\nLoot |\nAlways |\nEnt Leaves (100G/Green A) x 1d |\n2 - 4 |\nNothing |\n5 - 8 |\nMysterious Seeds (100G/Green A) |\n9+ |\nMysterious Sapling (500G/Green A) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Living Tree","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"xNdmnEXlJUArv42a","name":"Killer Cedar","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:killer-cedar","level":7,"monsterType":"Plant","intelligence":"None","perception":"Magic","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Forests, Lakesides, Caves","reputation":13,"weakness":16,"weakPoint":"Fire Damage +3","initiative":12,"movementSpeed":"10 (Multiple Legs/-)","fortitude":"10 (17)","willpower":"8 (15)","source":"BM","description":"A huge coniferous tree that can reach up to 10 meters in length. They posses the ability to walk on their roots and can appear in places beyond just forests. They indiscriminately attack enemies that come within its branches, and they further defend themselves by scattering pollen to create Poison Pollens .","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Poison, Disease, Psychic Immunity","description":"Trunk"},{"title":"► Twin Strike &amp; Double Action","description":"The Killer Cedar attacks twice with countless roots. After the results of the first attack are determined, the target for the second attack can be decided.\nBranch"},{"title":"◯ Painful Strike","description":"If the 2d roll of the damage roll is 10 or more, the damage is increased by an additional +6 points."},{"title":"► Poison Pollen Production","description":"The Killer Cedar shakes its branches and spawns a Poison Pollen . Once created, the Poison Pollen can immediately take its turn.\nThis ability cannot be used by the same Branch section in consecutive turns, nor can it be used by more than one Branch section on the same turn.\nWhen this ability is used, the Branch section that uses it loses 10 HP.\n2d |\nLoot |\nAlways |\nHard Tree Bark (330G / Green A) |\n2 - 8 |\nPollen Ball (60G / Green B) x 1d |\n9+ |\nPollen Ball (60G / Green B) x 2d |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Killer Cedar","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"y3NUMKqBHymSPfke","name":"Pondering Branch","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:pondering-branch","level":8,"monsterType":"Plant","intelligence":"High","perception":"Magic","disposition":"Neutral","soulscars":0,"languages":"Sylvan","habitat":"Forests","reputation":14,"weakness":19,"weakPoint":"Magic damage +2 points","initiative":15,"movementSpeed":"-","fortitude":"10 (17)","willpower":"11 (18)","source":"Natural History of Burlight p. 123","description":"This is a species of intelligent trees known as Entlets . These individuals have been discovered living deep in the forests of Kororopokka. They measure approximately 1.5 meters in length and have multiple branches, resembling tree branches with broad leaves.\n\nSometimes, they grow unnaturally directly from the ground, while other times, they cling to the wood of large trees like parasites. The dark green color of their leaves gives them a strong presence, and even without prior knowledge, one can intuitively sense that they are more than just ordinary tree branches.\n\nBeing contemplative creatures, they are often absorbed in philosophy. They possess a mild-mannered nature and, if approached peacefully, can offer valuable knowledge and advice. However, it is important to note that they have a tendency to speak in circles, so be prepared to listen attentively without becoming frustrated.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯2 Actions","description":"Can take two Major Actions in one round."},{"title":"►Green Transition","description":"Within Range/Area: 2(30m)/Target, will teleport itself to an arbitrary location (Simplified Combat: area, Standard/Advanced Combat: Coordinates), ignoring any movement restrictions by the skirmish area, movement obstructions, restraints, etc. The destination must be either the ground with visible soil or a tree trunk large enough for this monster to grow on."},{"title":"►Repulsion / 11 (19) / Willpower / Half","description":"Unleashes a force that blasts everything in its vicinity. Within \"Range: Caster,\" deals 2d+8 bludgeoning magic damage to \"Target: All Areas (20m Radius)/All.\"\nIn addition, a target that fails the Willpower Check is pushed far away and falls prone. The target will be pushed to the Rearguard area in Simplified Combat or 20m away from the target in Standard/Advanced Combat (in any direction, if the coordinates of the two are the same).\nUsing this effect consumes 8 MP.\n2d |\nLoot |\n2 - 5 |\nEnt Leaves (100G/Green A) |\n6 - 10 |\nEnt Leaves (100G/Green A) x 1d |\n11+ |\nEnt Leaves (100G/Green A) x 2d |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Pondering Branch","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"yuWWmtxlXOrt8vYY","name":"Nest Acacia","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:nest-acacia","level":3,"monsterType":"Plant","intelligence":"None","perception":"Magic","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Grasslands, Wilderness, Shallows","reputation":10,"weakness":12,"weakPoint":"Fire damage +3 points","initiative":10,"movementSpeed":"5 (Crawling)","fortitude":"5 (12)","willpower":"4 (11)","source":"AB, p. 94","description":"It is a tree that appears as a mass of leaves and thorns about 2 meters in diameter. It consists of branches, leaves, roots, and small purple flowers woven together in a basket-like form, and despite its appearance, it is light in weight - so much so that it can roll away in strong winds.\n\nWhile its self-propelled movement is minimal, this plant stores large amounts of sweet sap within its thorns, and animals gather to feed on it, rolling the plant around and thus expanding its habitat range. However, animals that die from being pierced by its sharp thorns become nutrients for the Nest Acacia.\n\nPurple Ants particularly favor this plant's nectar, and know how to extract the nectar without being pierced by the Nest Acacia's thorns. For some reason, after drinking the nectar, Purple Ants begin hunting other plants and animals to offer to the Nest Acacia.\n\nThe Nest Acacia sometimes becomes a \"mobile Purple Ant nest\" and may contain an Abyss Shard within its body. While a Nest Acacia's nectar is poisonous in its raw form, it can be processed for use in pharmaceuticals and food products.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯Psychic Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯Thorn Protection","description":"Any character attempting a melee attack against this monster receives 1 point of fixed damage each time, regardless of whether the attack succeeds or fails.\nPurple Ants are immune to this effect."},{"title":"►Poison Honey Spray / Can't","description":"Using this effect consumes 3 HP points from the user.\nSprays purple poison honey in \"Range: Caster\" with \"Target: 1 area (3m radius) / 5.\" Targets receive \"1d-3 (minimum 1)\" points of Poison magic damage. Inside a Shallow Abyss, the damage becomes \"1d-2 (minimum 1)\" points.\nIf the target is a Purple Ant, it receives no damage and instead recovers HP equal to the amount determined by the same calculation. This effect cannot be used in consecutive turns.\n2d |\nLoot |\nAlways |\nPurple Honey (40G/Green B) |\n2 - 11 |\nNothing |\n12+ |\nAbyss Shard (200G/-) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Nest Acacia","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"zrg1OjsgZ6eZYONg","name":"Tree Worm","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:tree-worm","level":11,"monsterType":"Plant","intelligence":"None","perception":"Magic","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Forests","reputation":20,"weakness":23,"weakPoint":"Fire damage +3 points","initiative":17,"movementSpeed":"15 (Crawling)","fortitude":"15 (22)","willpower":"12 (19)","source":"Natural History of Burlight p. 124","description":"This is a crawling plant native to the Burlight Region with a serpentine trunk that can reach over 1m in diameter and 20 to 25m in length. Its movement and silhouette resemble that of a giant snake or dragon. Despite being a vine, its body surface is covered with thorns and a tree-like hard skin that is resistant to damage from weapons.\n\nThe Tree Worm grows by preying on large animals, exhibiting several \"hunting\" mechanisms despite being a plant. Its tip is swollen and resembles the head of a snake or dragon from a distance. Inside, it is filled with seeds that can be sprayed. The roots coil up like a twisted rope during migration but spread wide when they feed on water or prey.\n\nTree Worm seeds are often dispersed immaturely, and most of them do not germinate. Due to their mobility, they are scattered and found over a wide area. These seeds are used as ingredients for \"Secret Tree Worm Medicine\" (See Natural History of Burlight, p. 41), which is sold at a reasonable price. Many people venture deep into the forest to collect them, but they face the risk of encountering various forest-dwelling animals or dangerous plants, especially the Tree Worm.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯Psychic Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯Pickable Seeds","description":""}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"Always","loot":"|"},{"roll":"2 - 11","loot":"|"},{"roll":"12+","loot":"|"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Tree Worm","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
